WEBVTT

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:17.540
Receiving mail...

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:18.250
Mail successfully received

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:18.250
OK

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:24.260
Mail successfully received

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.200
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.200
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.540
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.540
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.460
When fatigue strikes

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.460
suima ga yatte kite

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.090
My imagination runs wild

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.090
atama ga danshingu

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.550
Everything in life makes me smile

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.550
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.380
Nothing really new takes place

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.380
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.010
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.010
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.640
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.640
aozora peintingu

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.680
Where should we go?

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.680
doko ikou

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.270
Let's stay here

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.270
koko ni iyou

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.270
What's that?

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.270
sore wa nani

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.850
I wanna try that!

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.850
are yaritai

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.440
Let's make this moment count

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.440
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.820
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.820
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.490
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.490
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.950
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.950
nonbiri na everyday

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.580
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.580
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.410
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.410
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:39.000
So when your heart races in excitement

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:39.000
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.710
Just draw a sun at the top

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.710
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:46.840
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:46.840
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.180
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.180
gyutto shite ii kana

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.560
I've been sketching everything I love

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.560
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.100
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.100
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.860
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.860
sore ja ittekimasu

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:09.980
September 17th-19th,

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:09.980
Nazuna Meal

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.280
Ninety-one!

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.440
Ninety-two!

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.820
Yuno-san, are you there?

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.700
Oh, that must be...

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.750
Nazuna-chan, good morning!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.790
Morning!

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.210
Yuno-san, Miyako-san, good morning.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.590
Is something wrong?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.950
U-Um...

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:40.490
Can you teach me how to make fried chicken?

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:41.590
Fried chicken?

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.430
Yeah, I know how to make it, but why?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.380
I want to learn it by the day after tomorrow!

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.270
If I don't, I...

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:54.150
won't be able to face my parents!

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.980
Because of fried chicken?!

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.370
My parents are visiting the day after tomorrow.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.450
One of the main reasons they're coming to visit is to eat my cooking.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.830
Correct me if I'm wrong,

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.710
but aren't you a fine cook, Nazuna-dono?

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.630
I'm terrible.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:21.380
But I'm sure your parents will love it as long as you try your best.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:25.100
The thing is, when I went back home over the summer...

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.230
I told them I mastered the basics of cooking!

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:33.230
So...

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.630
My parents love fried chicken,

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:41.450
so I'd like to be able to make a meal centered
around that by the time they come over.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.740
I see. A meal, huh?

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.930
If you're fine with Japanese food,

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:49.200
I could show you how to make
miso soup and seasoned greens to go with it.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.750
That'd be perfect!

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.290
Thank you!

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.040
Guys!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.430
It'd be even more gorgeous with some Salisbury steak.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:00.170
It'd be gorgeous all right, but we can't just throw in a Western dish.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.640
Sushi, then!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.260
It takes years to learn how to make sushi.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.720
It's open!

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.060
I'm here!

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.470
Nori-chan?

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.020
I texted her to come over.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.020
Nazuna!

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.530
Why didn't you ask me?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.090
You see...

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.650
I did think about asking you,

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:29.090
but I realized my cooking would all be
Kansai-flavored if I were to learn from you.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.160
Isn't fried chicken all the same?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.460
What the heck is Kansai flavor anyway?

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.340
L-Like bonito and kelp?

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.210
Sorry!

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.310
Well, I have almost zero experience with fried foods,

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.970
so asking Yuno-san was the best choice anyway.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:48.760
I see.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.390
Have you considered asking Hiro-san?

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.690
She's a lot better than I am.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.770
I was afraid she might be busy studying.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.110
Let's go ask her now!

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.360
Oh, hey guys.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.860
U-Um...

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.210
Hiro-san, were you busy with school work?

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.240
Yes, I was drawing.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.650
Nazuna, what's going on?

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.790
U-Um...

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:22.840
Nazuna's parents are coming to Hidamari Apartments the day after tomorrow to taste her cooking.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:23.590
So...

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:28.070
Nazuna wants to make fried chicken
because both of her parents love them.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:29.070
Yes!

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:33.100
I wanted to ask you to teach me how to make them.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.010
Fried chicken? Sure thing!

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:38.610
For your parents, huh? You're a good daughter.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.610
Want to get started right away?

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.940
But aren't you busy with your drawing?

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.290
I've already drawn enough for today.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.450
Yeah, while I was asleep.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.700
There's a lot of drawings inside!

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.590
Wash the chicken legs in water, shake the water off,

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.340
cut it into bite-size pieces,

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.420
and marinate for about 20 minutes.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:12.510
Coat each piece in a mixture of equal amounts of flour and starch, then fry.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:18.060
Remove them just before they're done, and wait one minute.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.190
Then fry them again for a couple more minutes at high temperature.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.820
Once they look brown and crispy,

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.070
you're done!

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.820
What do you think?
You think you can make them now?

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.570
Sorry.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.590
I was so busy writing down the steps that I couldn't see what you were doing.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.830
Can you show me again?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.960
Tablespoon...

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.540
Can I use this one?

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.800
No, use this spoon!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:47.800
Hiro-san!

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.460
I couldn't slice the green onion right.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.140
They're still connected!

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:56.420
Nazuna-chan, how do you usually make your food?

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.390
Um...

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:01.020
Most of the time I just buy it from the deli at the supermarket.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.970
Then I arrange it on a plate, nice and neat.

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.400
<i>That's where you put forth the effort?</i>

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.610
I'm done!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.710
Oh, it's juicy and delicious!

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:18.750
You got it!

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.620
Thank you so much!

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.500
Now...

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.170
Yuno-sensei will teach you how to make miso soup!

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.500
Huh? Why me?

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:30.010
Because you make wonderful miso soup!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.010
What do you wanna do?

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:35.330
Should I get a bream head for the soup stock?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.760
L-Let's go with something more normal.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.690
Pour boiling water on a handful of dried bonito flakes and leave it for five minutes.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:45.550
Okay!

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:47.850
In the meantime, we can prepare the solid ingredients.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:51.010
Nazuna-chan, please put the dried seaweed in water.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:51.650
Got it!

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:56.470
Warm the bonito stock in the pot and add tofu.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.390
Make sure the fire's off when you're adding the miso.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.540
Y-Yuno-san!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.490
Look how much the seaweed blew up!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:15.050
To make seasoned spinach, first boil the spinach up from the roots.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:19.680
When it's all boiled, cool it with cold water.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.060
Then, shake off the water and soak it in the seasoning for about 30 minutes.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.730
Done!

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.370
And now you know how to make those three dishes!

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:31.250
What do you think? Do you think you'll be all right?

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.310
Yes, thank you so much!

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.570
Nice job!

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.070
<i>We</i> are not all right.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.130
I ended up eating too much.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.710
Can I get a doggy bag?

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.330
Good work, guys.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.960
Two days later!

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.090
Hello there!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.710
We're here!

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:54.470
Long time no see!

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:57.550
We'll see you again once you've had lunch.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:03.050
Nazuna-chan, what are you gonna cook for us today?

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:07.450
I thought I'd make fried chicken since you love it.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.110
Oh, I'm looking forward to it.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.850
She cooks for herself every day, right?

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.570
I see. How responsible of her.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.370
W-Well...

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:16.860
Hang in there!

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:20.130
Okay, just wait a bit.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:21.930
I've already gotten started on some of it,

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.230
so I don't think it'll take too long.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.750
Okay!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.250
You look so cute in your apron!

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.450
D-Do I?

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:32.250
Yeah, you look great!

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:36.010
Nazuna, you're not going to use a cookbook?

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.510
She must be a pro by now.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:39.760
Let's see...

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:43.260
<i>Coat each piece of the meat carefully in flour.</i>

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.610
I wonder if Nazuna-chan is doing all right.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.810
Yeah, I can't help but feel nervous.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.750
At the very least, I don't hear any screaming.

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:54.570
We'd have a real situation on our hands if we did.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.790
Miyako-san, can I have some tea?

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:02.010
Oh, sorry for not putting out any drinks.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.160
There's some in the fridge.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.450
Can I open it?

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.910
By all means, go ahead.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:11.610
Fried chicken...

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:16.250
Thankfully, it doesn't look like I'll run out anytime soon.

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:17.750
Would you like some with your tea?

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.340
No, thanks. I don't even want to look at them right now.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.770
Nazuna's going to text us if everything goes well, right?

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.600
Yes.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.270
Oh, it's her!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:34.030
The subject line is "Aaaaaaah."

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:36.480
Things don't look good.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.250
"Help me.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:40.930
I messed up cooking the rice."

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.410
What?!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.650
Excuse me!

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:47.120
I'm sorry!

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.610
It's so dry and hard.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.930
You didn't put in the right amount of water.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.380
Do I need to cook it all over again?

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.030
Let's make porridge.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:03.720
It's quick and easy, and since we already have side dishes, it won't need much flavor.

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.220
Thank you so much!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:11.400
It'll swell up, so two bowls of rice should be enough.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.210
Okay!

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:13.770
Do you have chicken soup base?

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.480
Um, probably.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.110
It's so delicious!

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.070
Yeah! It's wonderful!

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.080
That's great!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.650
You got everybody to help out, right?

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.330
Thank you, girls.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.920
Looks like you've got it made, Nazuna.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.250
Well, I figured that out pretty quickly.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.770
Huh? You did?

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:38.670
How could you tell?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:42.180
See, when you were cutting tofu and spinach,

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.430
you used a fruit knife!

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.560
Thanks for visiting me.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.050
What are you talking about?

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:54.170
You don't need to thank us for visiting our own daughter.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:56.670
You seem to be doing well, so we're relieved.

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.990
We were worried about letting you live alone,

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:01.400
but I'm glad to see that you're getting along well with your neighbors.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.210
Yeah!

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:05.610
I'm having a great time with the other girls at Hidamari Apartments.

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.330
Mom, you keep getting along well with Dad too!

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.830
Yer such a nice lil' girl now.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:16.330
When I move back after mah work's dun, let's all live together again!

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.380
You should also get rid of that accent when you move back, okay?

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:22.490
Did I let my accent slip?

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:23.380
Yeah.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.990
Nazuna, don't forget to thank those girls later!

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:30.140
Share our gift with them too!

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.430
Got it!

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:37.270
Everyone, thank you so much for today.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:41.050
My mom and dad were happy thanks to you.

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:43.430
You worked hard too.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.490
I wouldn't have thought of making porridge right away.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.910
You're so amazing, Hiro-san!

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:51.930
You surprised us with that text.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.190
Yuno-san, I want to thank you too.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:58.110
My dad said he loved the rich flavor of the miso soup.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:02.170
Well, yeah, you put a lot of effort into that miso soup.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:04.850
Nori-chan, Miyako-san, Sae-san,

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:08.430
thank you for taste-testing so much of my fried chicken.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.450
I'm glad I could help.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.930
I'm always up for doing delicious favors!

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:18.830
This is a gift from my parents for everyone.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.150
Awesome! What is it?

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:25.700
I don't know what's inside, but it's probably Nagoya's...

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.430
Fried chicken?!

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.050
Yay!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.510
They should last for a while,

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.210
so should we save them for later?

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.790
L-Let's do that.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:46.750
Today was intense.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:50.140
But I'm glad I got to make my parents smile.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:52.140
I guess...

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:56.990
you really need to cook every day to get good at it.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:03.730
I hope that eventually I can cook everything by myself.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.570
For breakfast tomorrow, instead of bread,

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:11.240
I should wake up early and try cooking rice and miso soup!

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.000
September 17th-19th

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.000
The End

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.000
To Be Continued

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:48.550
Just a dream, huh?

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:50.130
That was so scary.

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:51.780
Thank goodness it was just a dream.

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:56.030
It's two.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.230
It's Sae-san.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:14.680
That surprised me.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:18.030
"I knocked on the wall since I heard your voice."

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:20.270
"But it seems that I surprised you. Sorry."

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.330
"Are you all right?"

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.680
"Did something happen?"

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.530
Sorry for waking you up.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:30.230
I just woke up from a scary dream.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.290
"Oh, that must've been rough."

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.410
"Are you all right now?"

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.530
"Want to come over for a snack?"

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.830
Thank you for being so thoughtful.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.230
I'm all right.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:47.110
Sure, it was a scary dream, but...

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:50.210
It'd be faster to just talk to her.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:58.140
September 28th

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:58.140
Hyper Midnight

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.490
Welcome.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.010
Excuse me.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:04.270
Sorry for disturbing you this late at night.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.590
Don't mind it. I invited you.

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.690
Is bottled tea fine with you?

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:09.770
Oh, sure.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.780
Do you want to talk about your dream right now?

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.900
Or would you rather not since it's past two?

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:20.550
Sae-san, you sound like a granny.

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:21.530
Gran...

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:22.280
So?

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.530
What do you want to do?

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:27.150
They say dreams don't come true when you tell people about them.

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:29.040
Oh, I'll tell you the story.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.040
<i>You're sounding like a granny again.</i>

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:36.130
In the dream, I was drawing a picture on my computer,

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:40.800
but the picture had dull colors and had a creepy feel to it.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:45.180
Still, I kept working on that picture the best I could.

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:48.600
And when I was finally done, suddenly...

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.110
Suddenly?

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.170
The computer froze up, and I couldn't save it.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:58.270
And I hadn't saved any backups!

00:16:58.270 --> 00:17:00.740
<i>So it wasn't about the creepy feel of the picture?</i>

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:06.120
That was the dream, so I would've been fine just sitting in my room alone.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.030
I see. Too bad.

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:08.870
What's too bad?

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:13.630
I thought it was adorable when you said you woke up from a scary dream.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:16.820
What? You found it amusing?

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:18.510
I wouldn't go that far.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:22.770
There's a woman with long hair outside the window right now!

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.260
Not falling for it.

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:26.020
Look!

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:26.930
A centipede!

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:33.360
Anyway, I'm sorry I woke you up.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:36.630
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:37.810
I was awake.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:40.570
You were still awake?

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:42.490
Yeah.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.870
I was getting some work done.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.530
You use that, Sae-san?

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:49.010
What, this dictionary?

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.250
I do. Why?

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:53.590
You should just get a netbook.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:55.250
Is it a kind of book that makes your life easier?

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.550
It's not a book!

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:01.190
Netbooks are small laptops.

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:02.890
They're easy to carry around,

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:05.670
and they're super-convenient when you want to look up stuff or check e-mail.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:08.890
You can look up any word on the Internet with a single search, you know!

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.640
So you were talking about small laptops.

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.150
Buy one!

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:16.320
I've always thought paper dictionaries are inefficient.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.070
No,

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:19.310
it's not just about efficiency.

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:22.530
Actually this is more efficient for me.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:24.630
<i>More</i> efficient?

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:28.080
You can't compare the two if you haven't tried using a computer.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.830
You too. You're acting like this is automatically inefficient,

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:34.080
but have you ever used a paper dictionary regularly?

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:36.090
Do you know what's so great about them?

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:39.800
There's no way it could be efficient!

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.050
But Nori makes a good point.

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.050
But Sae-san makes a good point.

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:48.710
Sorry.

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:51.350
I shouldn't just disregard options without trying them.

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:53.220
I'll think about it.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:54.190
Thanks for the suggestion.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.130
I'd like to apologize too.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:58.320
I was so dead set on it that I ended up imposing it on you.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:02.890
I guess I'm more mature since I was the first to apologize?

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:04.650
What? That doesn't make sense.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:06.320
We pretty much apologized at the same time!

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:09.170
I'm more grown up!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:10.950
No sticking out your chest!

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:14.410
Sae-san, let me see your dictionary.

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.330
How do you use it?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.370
Sure thing.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:20.210
I highlight it using two colors.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.490
Wow!

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:25.570
You made a lot of notes in here.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:26.420
Yeah.

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:30.970
It's more effort, but I really feel like I remember things better when I look them up manually.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:33.870
Oh.

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.350
I see why you'd prefer this.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.110
Nori, are you feeling hungry?

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.110
Want some snacks?

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:42.670
Oh, I'll pass.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:44.670
Eating before bed makes me fat.

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:45.950
Wow, amazing.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:49.250
You're really mature and disciplined.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:52.150
I don't feel like I'm talking to someone younger when I talk to you.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:53.040
Is that so?

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.250
Especially considering that you're the same age as Chika.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.130
Maybe it's because you've been living alone.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.530
Oh, that's part of it.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.410
It definitely makes you self-reliant.

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:06.810
There's no one to give you food, clean your room, or do your laundry, after all.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.300
It makes you appreciate your parents a lot.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:13.130
There's a lot of freedom, like how there's no one to yell at you even if you stay up all night.

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:16.440
If I'm not disciplined, I'll keep getting sloppier.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.170
Yeah.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:22.530
I wonder if Chika would become mature like you if she moves out.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:25.670
Chika-chan commutes to her high school from home, right?

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:26.700
Yeah.

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:31.830
But I'd be so worried if she were to live by herself.

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:38.080
Sae-san, you really care a lot about Chika-chan, don't you?

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:42.130
Oh no, not quite.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:44.480
I want to hang out with Chika-chan again!

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:46.510
Thanks. I'll tell her.

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:49.890
Then she's staying at your room when she comes over next time, okay?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:50.750
What?

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.390
You're sisters, so you should stay together.

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.650
Sae?

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.400
Sae?

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.330
Sae?

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.690
Nori, wake up! We overslept!

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:19.910
I'm having a wonderful dream right now.

00:21:19.910 --> 00:21:21.750
Nori, Hiro's here.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.690
What? Hiro-san?

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:25.000
Huh? What time is it?

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:28.050
Whoa, I'm so sorry, Sae-san!

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.390
Do you think you'll make it to school?

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.770
Yes!

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:44.020
I'm back.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:46.970
I should have time for a quick shower.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:57.910
All right!

00:21:57.910 --> 00:21:59.430
I'm all awake now!

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:00.790
Today's going to be great!

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:03.750
Right!

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:06.000
I need to hurry, or I'll be late for school!

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:15.220
Hidamari dice roll talk's starting!

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:16.440
Do you like Salisbury steak?

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:17.860
What happened there?!

00:22:17.860 --> 00:22:19.440
I like gratin!

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:21.020
Are all the topics about food?

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:21.740
Then...

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:23.240
Something you can only say right now.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.540
That's tough.

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:25.800
I can't think of any.

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:26.780
How about you, Hiro-san?

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:29.020
Sorry. I can't say it yet.

00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:29.700
What?!

00:22:30.020 --> 00:22:33.340
Next time: "September 25th, Chatter Sketch."

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:36.420
"September 29th-30th, Hiro-san."

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:39.960
We'll be waiting at Yamabuki High School, so come visit us!
